From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iphlpapi: change addresses, routes and neighbour entries through sg-netctl

Create/Delete/SetUnicastIpAddressEntry, Create/Delete/SetIpForwardEntry2,
Create/Delete/SetIpNetEntry2, FlushIpNetTable2, FlushIpPathTable and the
anycast pair were not implemented; the older AddIPAddress, DeleteIPAddress,
Create/Delete/SetIpForwardEntry, Create/Delete/SetIpNetEntry and
FlushIpNetTable were stubs.

All of them need an administrator (the Administrators group in the caller's
token) and fail with ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED otherwise. After the arguments are
checked they become sg-netctl requests (addr add|del, route add|del|set,
neigh add|del|flush), the interface named by its Linux name; sg-netctl's
refusal kinds map to ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED, ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER,
ERROR_NOT_FOUND, ERROR_OBJECT_ALREADY_EXISTS (exists), ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED and
ERROR_GEN_FAILURE, and every call, the older ones too, returns that real
result. Only with no sg-netctl at all (a plain Wine) do the new calls fail with
ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED and the older ones, which used to say NO_ERROR without
doing anything, still say it. Anycast addresses are ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED, and
there is no path cache to flush.
